// ============================================================
//
// ### Commands::Command ###
//	Name: Text typed in the chat, starts with / and has no spaces, letter case does not matter, each Name only once in the file
//	Id: Command of the GameServer run by the Name, several Names may use the same Id (aliases, e.g. translations: /post and /wiadomosc)
//	Authority: Who may use the Name, optional, the minimum of the Id when missing
//		~ 0: Every player
//		~ 1: Game Master (CtlCode 8) and Administrator (CtlCode 32)
//		~ 2: Administrator only (CtlCode 32)
//
//	A value below the minimum of the Id is raised to the minimum, the GameServer log says so
//	Commands removed from the file cannot be used
//	Game Master commands also need the privilege flag in IGC.EssentialTool, GM Management, named in the comment of the entry
//	Reload on the GameServer console: data.reload.commands
//
// ### Item parameters ###
//	/item <group> <index> <level> <durability> <skill> <luck> <option> <exc> <setitem> <periodtime> <socketslot> <socketbonus/attribute> <muunevolutionitemcat> <muunevolutionitemindex>
//	group, index: ItemList.xml
//	level: 0-15
//	durability: 0 = default durability, overlap value for overlap items
//	skill, luck: 0/1
//	option: 0-7, option * 4 = item option
//	exc: Excellent options
//		~ -1: No excellent option
//		~ -2: Random count of random options, rates from ExcellentOptions.xml
//		~ -3;X: X random options, max 9, rates from ExcellentOptions.xml
//		~ X;X;X;X;X;X;X;X;X: Option IDs from ExcellentOptions.xml, max 9
//
//	exc: Grade options of 4th wings
//		~ -1: No grade option
//		~ -2: Random count of random options, rates from ItemGradeOption.xml
//		~ -3;X: X random options, max 4
//		~ ID1;LV1;ID2;LV2;ID3;LV3;ID4;LV4: Index and GradeXVal level (0-9) from ItemGradeOption.xml, max 4
//
//	exc: Guardian items
//		~ -1: No option
//		~ -2;X: Random count of random options from GuardianItemOption.xml, X = 0/1 random elite option
//		~ -3;X;Y: X random options, max 4, Y = 0/1 random elite option
//		~ X;X;X;X;Y: OptionList indexes, max 4, -1 if not applies, Y = EliteOptionList index or -1
//
//	exc: Artifact items
//		~ -1: No option
//		~ -2: Random option set, rates from ArtifactSystem.xml
//		~ X1;Y1;X2;Y2;X3;Y3: X = OptionType from ArtifactOption.xml, Y = value index 1-10, -1 if not applies
//
//	exc: Ability cards
//		~ -1: Random option
//		~ X: Option index from AbilityCardOption.xml
//		~ X;Y: Option index from AbilityCardOption.xml and add option index from AbilityCardAddOption.xml
//
//	setitem: Ancient option, the item must be set in ItemSetType.xml
//		~ 0: No set item
//		~ 5: Tier 1 +5 Stamina
//		~ 6: Tier 2 +5 Stamina
//		~ 9: Tier 1 +10 Stamina
//		~ 10: Tier 2 +10 Stamina
//		~ 20: Tier 3 +5 Stamina
//		~ 24: Tier 4 +5 Stamina
//		~ 36: Tier 3 +10 Stamina
//		~ 40: Tier 4 +10 Stamina
//
//	periodtime: Expiration in seconds, not every item supports it
//	socketslot: Count of empty socket slots, socket and pentagram items
//	socketbonus/attribute: Socket bonus of a socket item, or pentagram element
//		~ 0: No attribute
//		~ 1: Fire
//		~ 2: Water
//		~ 3: Earth
//		~ 4: Wind
//		~ 5: Darkness
//
//	muunevolutionitemcat, muunevolutionitemindex: Muun of the Evolution Stone (13,211) only
//
// ### GremoryGift parameters ###
//	/addgift <name> <storage> <group> <index> <level> <durability> <skill> <luck> <option> <exc> <setitem> <socketslot> <socketbonus/attribute> <muunevolutionitemcat> <muunevolutionitemindex> <days>
//	storage: Gremory Case storage
//		~ 1: Server
//		~ 2: Character
//
//	Other parameters as in Item parameters, days = days to expire
//
// ### Spawn parameters ###
//	/spawn <class> <map> <range> <x> <y> <regen> <regen_time>
//	class: MonsterList.xml
//	map: MapList.xml, -1 = current map
//	range: Spawn range in tiles from x, y
//	x, y: Position 1-255, own position + 2 when missing on the own map
//	regen: 0/1, respawn after death
//	regen_time: Seconds to respawn, regen 1 only
//
// STRICTLY NO COMMENTS INSIDE TAGS
-->

